{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Api-Eks-2017-11-01","context":"### InsightCategorySpecificSummary\n\n##### Description\n\nSummary information that relates to the category of the insight. Currently only returned with certain insights having category `UPGRADE_READINESS`.\n\n##### Members\n\n**addonCompatibilityDetails**\n: : **Type:** *Array of AddonCompatibilityDetail structures*\n\n A list of `AddonCompatibilityDetail` objects for Amazon EKS add-ons.\n\n**deprecationDetails**\n: : **Type:** *Array of DeprecationDetail structures*\n\n The summary information about deprecated resource usage for an insight check in the `UPGRADE_READINESS` category","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-sdk-php/v3/api/api-eks-2017-11-01.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"InsightsFilter","context":"## Contents\n\n**categories**\n: The categories to use to filter insights. The following lists the available categories:\n\n * `UPGRADE_READINESS`: Amazon EKS identifies issues that could impact your\n ability to upgrade to new versions of Kubernetes. These are called upgrade insights.\n * `MISCONFIGURATION`: Amazon EKS identifies misconfiguration in your EKS\n Hybrid Nodes setup that could impair functionality of your cluster or\n workloads. These are called configuration insights.\n\n Type: Array of strings\n\n Valid Values: `UPGRADE_READINESS | MISCONFIGURATION | ROLLBACK_READINESS`\n\n Required: No\n\n**kubernetesVersions**\n: The Kubernetes versions to use to filter the insights.\n\n Type: Array of strings\n\n Required: No\n\n**statuses**\n: The statuses to use to filter the insights.\n\n Type: Array of strings\n\n Valid Values: `PASSING | WARNING | ERROR | UNKNOWN`\n\n Required: No","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/APIReference/API_InsightsFilter.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Amazon EKS introduces upgrade insights","context":"# Amazon EKS introduces upgrade insights\n\nPosted On: Dec 20, 2023\n\nToday, Amazon EKS announces the general availability of upgrade insights, a new feature that surfaces insights about issues that may impact your ability to successfully upgrade a cluster to newer versions of Kubernetes. Upgrade insights are built upon best practices learned by EKS over the course of managing hundreds of thousands of Kubernetes clusters. You can use the EKS APIs and Console to check for upgrade readiness issues detected in your environment at any time against all future Kubernetes versions supported by EKS.\n\nKubernetes is a fast-paced, evolving open source project with 3 releases per year, making upgrades a routine part of running Kubernetes clusters. EKS upgrade insights automatically scan clusters against a list of potential Kubernetes version upgrade impacting issues. EKS periodically updates the list of insight checks to perform, based on evaluations of changes in the Kubernetes project, as well as changes introduced in the EKS service along with new versions. EKS upgrade insights surface issues and provide remediation recommendations, accelerating the testing and verification process for upgrades to newer versions of Kubernetes.\n\nStatus of EKS upgrade insights can be viewed starting today for all EKS clusters in all AWS Regions, except the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions, China (Beijing, operated by Sinnet) Region, and China (Ningxia, operated by NWCD) Region. To get started visit the EKS documentation. To learn more about the feature, see the launch blog","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-eks-upgrade-insights/"}]}}

## Recent AWS announcements (What's New)

Newer than your training data may be. When these conflict with the documentation results above or with what you remember, prefer the most recent dated source.

{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon EKS expands catalog of upgrade insight checks - AWS","context":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) has introduced new enhancements to its upgrade insights feature. This feature identifies potential issues that could impact the successful upgrade of a Kubernetes cluster to a newer version. The new enhancements enable EKS to scan and warn on health and version compatibility issues between various Kubernetes components, including kubelet, kube-proxy, and EKS add-ons. Kubernetes undergoes frequent releases, making upgrades a regular process","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2024/12/amazon-eks-catalog-upgrade-insights-checks/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon EKS now supports Kubernetes version rollback - AWS","context":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) now offers Kubernetes version rollback, allowing users to revert to the previous minor version within 7 days of an upgrade. This feature provides an extra layer of safety during upgrades, enabling validation of new versions under production conditions and the option to rollback if necessary. Users can initiate a rollback through the Amazon EKS console, AWS CLI, or AWS SDKs. Before initiating a rollback, Amazon EKS evaluates readiness insights, including API compatibility, version skew, add-on compatibility, and cluster health. For clusters using EKS Auto Mode, Amazon EKS automatically manages the rollback of worker nodes and reverts the control plane, adhering to disruption controls. Amazon EKS version rollback is available at no additional cost in all regions where Amazon EKS is offered. To get started, refer to the version rollback section in the Amazon EKS User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/amazon-eks-version-rollback/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"What's New at AWS - Cloud Innovation & News","context":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS) has introduced on-demand refresh of cluster insights. This new feature allows customers to immediately fetch the latest insights after making changes to their clusters, accelerating the testing and verification process during upgrades or configuration changes. EKS undergoes automatic, periodic checks against a curated list of insights, which provide detection of issues and recommendations for addressing them. These insights include warnings before Kubernetes version upgrades. The on-demand cluster insights refresh capability is available in all commercial AWS Regions. For more information, visit the EKS documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/08/amazon-eks-on-demand-insights-refresh/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"amazon-keyspaces","skill_description":"Provides authoritative compatibility checks, pricing estimates, connection troubleshooting, pre-warming guidance, and infrastructure mutations for Amazon Keyspaces (for Apache Cassandra). Covers LWT/batch operations, secondary indexes, materialized views, capacity modes, TTL, PITR, CDC, auto-scaling, multi-region keyspaces, UDTs, nodetool diagnostics parsing, SQL-to-Cassandra migration, and Cassandra-to-Keyspaces migration scenarios. Agents frequently produce incomplete or incorrect answers about Keyspaces feature support without this skill loaded.\n\nServices: keyspaces, cassandra\nTasks: cost-estimation, migration-assessment, compatibility-check, data-modeling, create, modify\nPersona: developer, devops, architect, dba\nWorkload: nosql, wide-column-store, cassandra-migration\n*","skill_name":"amazon-keyspaces"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"aws-containers","skill_description":"Builds, deploys, debugs, and optimizes containerized workloads on Amazon EKS, ECS, Fargate, ECR, and Elastic Beanstalk. Covers EKS operations and add-ons; ECS task definitions, services, Exec, Express Mode, Managed Instances, and Action Logs; ECR repositories and lifecycle policies; and Elastic Beanstalk platforms plus Beanstalk Cluster Mode for running containerized applications on service-managed EKS compute. Use for container deployment, service selection, configuration, scaling, health, troubleshooting, image workflows, or deciding between Beanstalk-managed Cluster Mode and direct EKS. Should be used instead of relying on internal knowledge for these services.\n\nServices: ecs, ecr, eks, apprunner, beanstalk\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: containers, compute, kubernetes\n*","skill_name":"aws-containers"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS docs on EKS Cluster Insights categories and naming"}
